# Citation metadata (https://citation-file-format.github.io/), read by
# GitHub's "Cite this repository" box and by Zenodo's GitHub integration when
# a release is archived. `version` and `date-released` are deliberately
# omitted: Zenodo takes both from the release itself, and a hand-maintained
# copy here would only drift (RELEASING.md).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use limen, please cite it as below. Report the package version AND the
  rulings-spec version your numbers were produced under (`limen env` prints
  both): a rulings-spec change means a recorded measurement meaning changed.
title: "limen: the same-configuration noise floor of an evaluation"
abstract: >-
  limen is an analyzer over repeated identical evaluation runs: per-item
  verdict flakiness (the pairwise-disagreement U-statistic, with the
  constant-verdict fraction as an explicit upper bound on TARa@N), per-pair
  SIGN-STABLE/SIGN-UNSTABLE rulings over single-draw leaderboards, the minimum
  detectable difference at the observed number of repeats (after Kalibera and
  Jones), a stable-items-only re-ranking shipped only with its selection-bias
  mitigations, a drift guard whose missing-field state is never PASS, a
  grader-defect count, and a CI gate that fails a benchmark report claiming a
  gain smaller than that report's own measured draw noise. It makes no
  statement about which model is better.
type: software
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KurathSec/limen"
url: "https://kurathsec.github.io/limen/"
authors:
  - given-names: "Yuxiang"
    family-names: "Ji"
    affiliation: "Sunway College"
    email: "kurathandrew@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-9835-3800"
keywords:
  - "evaluation"
  - "reproducibility"
  - "flakiness"
  - "noise floor"
  - "benchmark"
  - "rank stability"
  - "measurement instrument"
  - "large language models"
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Spaghetti Architect"
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21033174"
    authors:
      - given-names: "Yuxiang"
        family-names: "Ji"
    notes: >-
      Source of the committed repeated-draw archives and deterministic graders
      from which limen's frozen calibration corpus is derived, read-only
      (calibration/spaghetti/, NOTICE).
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "Non-Determinism of \"Deterministic\" LLM Settings"
    authors:
      - given-names: "Berk"
        family-names: "Atil"
    year: 2024
    notes: >-
      arXiv:2408.04667 (Atil et al.). Defines TARa@N; limen's constant-verdict
      fraction is reported as an explicit upper bound on it, under this
      citation, never under the metric's name outright.
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "Rigorous benchmarking in reasonable time"
    authors:
      - given-names: "Tomas"
        family-names: "Kalibera"
      - given-names: "Richard"
        family-names: "Jones"
    collection-title: "Proceedings of the 2013 International Symposium on Memory Management (ISMM 2013)"
    year: 2013
    doi: "10.1145/2464157.2464160"
    notes: >-
      Source of the minimum-detectable-difference construction limen
      specializes to one repetition level; cited in every MDD block rather
      than reinvented.
